'''Dhaalu Airport''' {{airport codes|DDD|VRMU}} is an [[international airport]] located on the island of [[Kudahuvadhoo]] in [[Dhaalu Atoll]] in the [[Maldives|Republic of Maldives]]. It was built by Reollo Investments Pvt. Ltd. and is operated by Dhaalu Airport Holdings.

==History==

The airport began operations in 2017, with the first aircraft landing at Dhaalu Airport on June 1, 2017.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://english.sun.mv/43803|title=First plane lands in Kudahuvadhoo airport - A dream come true for the people|work=Sun Online|access-date=2017-06-26}}</ref> International flights will be started from this airport to [[India]] in January 2024.

==Facilities==
The airport was built entirely on 63 hectares of reclaimed land and features a runway of 1,800 metres allowing it to accommodate [[Bombardier Dash 8|Dash-8]] and [[ATR 72|ATR-72]]  aircraft<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://en.mihaaru.com/maldives-to-unveil-dhaalu-atoll-domestic-airport-next-week/|title=Maldives to unveil Dhaalu atoll domestic airport next week – Mihaaru|website=en.mihaaru.com|language=en-US|access-date=2017-06-26|archive-date=2017-07-18|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170718112649/http://en.mihaaru.com/maldives-to-unveil-dhaalu-atoll-domestic-airport-next-week/|url-status=dead}}</ref> as well as large private jets.

Dhaalu Airport is the first airport in Maldives to make extensive use of solar airfield lighting.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://solutions4ga.com/project/dhaalu_airport/|title=Dhaalu Airport - Maldives - S4GA|work=S4GA|access-date=2017-06-26|language=en-US}}</ref>

Currently, [[Manta Air]] is the only airline offering scheduled service at the airport.

